Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The previous attempt to ship this (commit fefaee7, "Ledger PDF layout +
website") didn't actually apply — ledger-pdf-layout.patch was missing
from the folder it was applied from, so `git apply` failed on it, and
the follow-up ledger-website.patch failed too since its context depended
on the first patch already being applied. `git add -A` then picked up
and committed the stray ledger-website.patch file itself instead of any
real change. This commit removes that stray file and actually contains
the intended changes, combined into one commit this time.

Add exportLedgerStatementPdf: a company letterhead (name/address/GSTIN/
UDYAM/website), a party block with the dealer's own name/address/GSTIN
(from profiles.gstin via get_dealer_detail — real data, omitted when a
dealer has none on file), the period, then a fully-bordered ledger table
with a Vch Type column, an Opening Balance row, every voucher with its
running Balance, and Total/Closing Balance rows — replacing the old bare
flat table. Wired into both the Ledger tab's own export and the Overview
tab's "Statement PDF" button.

